1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,657
Cabinets come from the library. Click Add cabinet to see the presets.

2
00:00:07,657 --> 00:00:10,637
This shop saved US-size presets: bases 34-1/2" high and 24" deep.

3
00:00:10,637 --> 00:00:13,673
Start at the left end with an 18" 3-drawer base.

4
00:00:13,673 --> 00:00:18,733
Next, a 24" 2-door base...

5
00:00:18,733 --> 00:00:23,787
...the 36" sink base for the middle...

6
00:00:23,787 --> 00:00:33,722
...then the same again in reverse, so the run is symmetric.

7
00:00:33,722 --> 00:00:36,714
Five bases, numbered B1 to B5 in the order they were added.

8
00:00:36,714 --> 00:00:40,238
Now place them. Open the Room tab.

9
00:00:40,238 --> 00:00:44,661
Arrange along the back wall sets them out from the left corner, in list order.

10
00:00:44,661 --> 00:00:53,020
Side by side against the wall, with the sink in the middle.

11
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,955
Plan view, looking down: the back wall is at the top, fronts are the thick edges.

12
00:00:56,955 --> 00:01:02,536
Drag a cabinet and it moves freely...

13
00:01:02,536 --> 00:01:08,612
...bring it back and Snap butts it against its neighbour and the wall (hold Alt to switch it off).

14
00:01:08,612 --> 00:01:11,798
B5 is back in line. Next: the wall cabinets above.
